---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro'
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro'
import { PUBLIC_PYPI_URL, PUBLIC_RELEASE_URL, PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION } from '../lib/public-release'

const title = 'Veqtor MCP Documentation — Tools, Workflow and Boundaries'
const description = `Technical overview of public Veqtor ${PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION}: nine tools, exact paragraph history, quotation projections, supported Word redlines and privacy boundaries.`
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/docs">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Documentation"
    title={`A technical map of public Veqtor ${PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION}.`}
    lede={`Start here for the v${PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} tool surface, operating model and assurance boundaries. Installation artifacts are available through the immutable public release.`}
    meta={`Public v${PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} · Nine tools · macOS and Linux`}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Documentation' }]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose-shell">
      <article class="prose">
        <section id="model">
          <h2>Operating model</h2>
          <p>Veqtor is a local MCP server using the stdio transport. Claude remains the model and reasoning layer. Veqtor exposes deterministic document operations for a narrow Word redline workflow.</p>
          <p>The server has no embedded model calls. Tool results enter the MCP client conversation and may be sent to the user’s model provider.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="tools">
          <h2>Veqtor {PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} tools</h2>
          <div class="tool-list">
            <article><code>list_rounds</code><h3>Discover negotiation drafts</h3><p>Scans one local folder, ignores Word lock files and reports readable rounds in deterministic filename order.</p></article>
            <article><code>extract_redlines</code><h3>Read supported tracked changes</h3><p>Returns change units, document hashes, structural references and bounded paragraph context.</p></article>
            <article><code>inspect_document</code><h3>Read accepted/current text</h3><p>Returns bounded main-body views with paragraph references bound to the exact document bytes.</p></article>
            <article><code>map_rounds</code><h3>Map exact cross-round evidence</h3><p>Reports exact paragraph equality and recorded document-byte derivations without inferring chronology or lineage.</p></article>
            <article><code>trace_paragraph_history</code><h3>Trace one paragraph across drafts</h3><p>Follows exact paragraph matches backward through the declared file order, using current text or a mechanical reading with supported pending text revisions rejected. Reports ambiguous and unresolved steps rather than guessing.</p></article>
            <article><code>verify_quote</code><h3>Check one quote at its source</h3><p>Compares supplied wording with a specific tracked change or hash-bound paragraph and returns exact, normalized or not_found. Paragraph checks use current text by default; rejected-pending text must be selected explicitly.</p></article>
            <article><code>preflight_edits</code><h3>Test the complete edit batch</h3><p>Runs the full document-processing pipeline in memory and never creates an output document.</p></article>
            <article><code>apply_edits</code><h3>Create a new tracked-change output</h3><p>Writes supported replace, delete, counter and reinstate edits atomically to a create-if-absent file.</p></article>
            <article><code>export_decision_record</code><h3>Export compact local provenance</h3><p>Returns a privacy-aware summary of the best-effort local activity journal for later review.</p></article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="sequence">
          <h2>Expected trust sequence</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>List the available rounds.</li>
            <li>Inspect the exact paragraph in the last declared file, then trace its history. Use the round map separately for navigation and recorded derivations.</li>
            <li>Extract the current redlines.</li>
            <li>Verify every quotation used as evidence.</li>
            <li>Preflight the complete proposed edit batch.</li>
            <li>Apply only when the batch is reported as applicable.</li>
            <li>Re-extract the output and export the decision record.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Veqtor never overwrites the source or an existing output file. A successful write creates a new Word document and normally appends to a private local journal.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="history">
          <h2>Paragraph history and quotation checks</h2>
          <p>Start with a paragraph reference from <code>inspect_document</code> in the last declared file. History uses either <code>filename_lexicographic_v1</code> or a complete <code>explicit_filename_sequence_v1</code> list without missing or duplicate files. Neither choice verifies chronology or lineage.</p>
          <p>The result is seed-first and follows exact matches backward. Ambiguity or an unresolved step stops further backward propagation; fuzzy or semantic matching is not performed. Returned change units belong only to the selected paragraph, not every change in the document.</p>
          <p>For <code>verify_quote</code>, paragraph references default to <code>accepted_current_v1</code>. Set <code>paragraph_projection</code> to <code>pending_text_revisions_rejected_v1</code> explicitly to check the mechanical reading with supported pending text revisions rejected. This is not a recovered original or necessarily the wording of a prior round, does not establish legal effect, and does not write or reject changes in Word. Use the returned <code>checked_projection</code> to identify what was checked.</p>
          <p>Author and date strings are literal Word metadata only. For example, an author value of <code>53</code> does not identify a person: <code>authorship_verified</code> and <code>time_verified</code> remain <code>false</code>.</p>
          <p>History pages default to 50 observations, with a maximum of 100. Follow <code>next_cursor</code> until it is null; an observation is never split. Files, seed, order, policies and result must remain unchanged between pages. A complete page is not proof that all pages were retrieved.</p>
          <div class="notice"><strong>One contract version for all nine tools.</strong><p>v0.4 advertises <code>veqtor.mcp.v0.4</code> on every tool, including the eight existing names. Clients pinned to <code>veqtor.mcp.v0.3</code> must deliberately adopt the new contract; this is not merely an extra tool under the old version.</p></div>
        </section>

        <section id="records">
          <h2>Local decision records</h2>
          <p>Unless disabled, tool calls append JSON Lines records to <code>&lt;matter&gt;/.veqtor/decision-records.jsonl</code>. The raw journal may contain verbatim matter text and should not be committed or shared.</p>
          <p>These records are best-effort local provenance. They are not authenticated, signed, hash-chained or tamper-evident. Always check <code>record_status</code> before treating an operation as durably recorded.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="primary-docs">
          <h2>Primary documentation and release status</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={`${PUBLIC_RELEASE_URL.replace('/releases/tag/', '/blob/')}/README.md`}>Tagged README and version-selection rule</a></li>
            <li><a href={`${PUBLIC_RELEASE_URL.replace('/releases/tag/', '/blob/')}/API.md`}>Tagged v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} MCP tool API</a></li>
            <li><a href={`${PUBLIC_RELEASE_URL.replace('/releases/tag/', '/blob/')}/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md`}>Tagged v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} known limitations</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/JohnDeer-ai/veqtor-mcp/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security policy and threat model</a></li>
            <li><a href={PUBLIC_RELEASE_URL}>Immutable public v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} release and artifacts</a></li>
            <li><a href={PUBLIC_PYPI_URL}>Public v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} package on PyPI</a></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="notice notice--lime"><strong>The tagged v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION} contract is public.</strong><p>The immutable release and its verified assets define the version users may install. Tagged documents retain their pre-publication checks and conditional version-selection rule; both public sources now expose v{PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERSION}. The default branch can continue to evolve after that release.</p></div>
        </section>
      </article>
      <aside class="side-index" aria-label="Documentation sections">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#model">Operating model</a>
        <a href="#tools">Public tools</a>
        <a href="#sequence">Trust sequence</a>
        <a href="#history">History &amp; quotations</a>
        <a href="#records">Decision records</a>
        <a href="#primary-docs">Primary documentation</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SiteCta title="New to Veqtor? Start with the visual workflow." primaryHref="/demo" primaryLabel="Watch the demo" secondaryHref="/setup" secondaryLabel="Connect Veqtor" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 64px; padding-top: 56px; }
  .tool-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  .tool-list article { display: grid; gap: 10px 22px; grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, .4fr) minmax(0, 1fr); padding: 22px 0; }
  .tool-list article + article { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tool-list code { align-self: start; color: var(--lime); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .tool-list h3 { font-size: 17px; margin: 0; }
  .tool-list p { grid-column: 2; margin: -4px 0 0; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .tool-list article { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .tool-list p { grid-column: 1; } }
</style>
